    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "In `mini.files`, I had the 'problem', that I wanted to exit with `<ESC>` _and_ `q`. I managed to have this behaviour with the following configuration. It would be a nice feature to have this as an option inside mini.files. When I am not alone, I could try to implement it.\r\n\r\n```lua\r\n      require(\"mini.files\").setup({\r\n        mappings = { close = \"<ESC>\" },\r\n      })\r\n      vim.api.nvim_create_autocmd({ \"BufEnter\" }, {\r\n        callback = function(ev)\r\n          if vim.bo[ev.buf].filetype == \"minifiles\" then\r\n            vim.api.nvim_buf_set_keymap(ev.buf, \"n\", \"q\", \":lua require('mini.files').close()<CR>\", {})\r\n          end\r\n        end,\r\n      })\r\n```",
    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">In <code class=\"notranslate\">mini.files</code>, I had the 'problem', that I wanted to exit with <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;ESC&gt;</code> <em>and</em> <code class=\"notranslate\">q</code>. I managed to have this behaviour with the following configuration. It would be a nice feature to have this as an option inside mini.files. When I am not alone, I could try to implement it.</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"      require(&quot;mini.files&quot;).setup({\n        mappings = { close = &quot;&lt;ESC&gt;&quot; },\n      })\n      vim.api.nvim_create_autocmd({ &quot;BufEnter&quot; }, {\n        callback = function(ev)\n          if vim.bo[ev.buf].filetype == &quot;minifiles&quot; then\n            vim.api.nvim_buf_set_keymap(ev.buf, &quot;n&quot;, &quot;q&quot;, &quot;:lua require('mini.files').close()&lt;CR&gt;&quot;, {})\n          end\n        end,\n      })\"><pre class=\"notranslate\">      <span class=\"pl-c1\">require</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>mini.files<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>).<span class=\"pl-c1\">setup</span>({\n        <span class=\"pl-smi\">mappings</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> { <span class=\"pl-smi\">close</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>&lt;ESC&gt;<span class=\"pl-pds\">\" </span></span>},\n      })\n      <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">api</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">nvim_create_autocmd</span>({ <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>BufEnter<span class=\"pl-pds\">\" </span></span>}, {\n        <span class=\"pl-en\">callback</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">ev</span>)\n          <span class=\"pl-k\">if</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">bo</span>[<span class=\"pl-smi\">ev</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">buf</span>].<span class=\"pl-e\">filetype</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">==</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>minifiles<span class=\"pl-pds\">\" </span></span><span class=\"pl-k\">then</span>\n            <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">api</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">nvim_buf_set_keymap</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">ev</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">buf</span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>n<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>q<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>:lua require('mini.files').close()&lt;CR&gt;<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>, {})\n          <span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>\n        <span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>,\n      })</pre></div>",
    "bodyText": "In mini.files, I had the 'problem', that I wanted to exit with <ESC> and q. I managed to have this behaviour with the following configuration. It would be a nice feature to have this as an option inside mini.files. When I am not alone, I could try to implement it.\n      require(\"mini.files\").setup({\n        mappings = { close = \"<ESC>\" },\n      })\n      vim.api.nvim_create_autocmd({ \"BufEnter\" }, {\n        callback = function(ev)\n          if vim.bo[ev.buf].filetype == \"minifiles\" then\n            vim.api.nvim_buf_set_keymap(ev.buf, \"n\", \"q\", \":lua require('mini.files').close()<CR>\", {})\n          end\n        end,\n      })",
