    "comment_count": 1,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author": {
                "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                "login": "echasnovski",
                "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion.\r\n\r\nThis won't be a part of 'mini.files' because buffers there are also meant to be edited inside Insert or Visual mode. Hence `<Esc>` original meaning is valuable.\r\n\r\nCreating own buffer-local mapping is a suggested approach here. The recommended approach is to follow [an example from help](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/6d1cbcaec421b3768088b4047e78ce22e5503b99/doc/mini-files.txt#L420-L427) and use dedicated 'mini.files' events. With something like this:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('User', {\r\n  pattern = 'MiniFilesBufferCreate',\r\n  callback = function(args)\r\n    vim.keymap.set('n', '<Esc>', function() MiniFiles.close() end, { buffer = args.data.buf_id, desc = 'Close' })\r\n  end,\r\n})\r\n```",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Thanks for the suggestion.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This won't be a part of 'mini.files' because buffers there are also meant to be edited inside Insert or Visual mode. Hence <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;Esc&gt;</code> original meaning is valuable.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Creating own buffer-local mapping is a suggested approach here. The recommended approach is to follow <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/6d1cbcaec421b3768088b4047e78ce22e5503b99/doc/mini-files.txt#L420-L427\">an example from help</a> and use dedicated 'mini.files' events. With something like this:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"vim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('User', {\n  pattern = 'MiniFilesBufferCreate',\n  callback = function(args)\n    vim.keymap.set('n', '&lt;Esc&gt;', function() MiniFiles.close() end, { buffer = args.data.buf_id, desc = 'Close' })\n  end,\n})\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">api</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">nvim_create_autocmd</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>User<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, {\n  <span class=\"pl-smi\">pattern</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>MiniFilesBufferCreate<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>,\n  <span class=\"pl-en\">callback</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">args</span>)\n    <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">keymap</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">set</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>n<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>&lt;Esc&gt;<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>() <span class=\"pl-smi\">MiniFiles</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">close</span>() <span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>, { <span class=\"pl-smi\">buffer</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">args</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">data</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">buf_id</span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">desc</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>Close<span class=\"pl-pds\">' </span></span>})\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>,\n})</pre></div>",
            "bodyText": "Thanks for the suggestion.\nThis won't be a part of 'mini.files' because buffers there are also meant to be edited inside Insert or Visual mode. Hence <Esc> original meaning is valuable.\nCreating own buffer-local mapping is a suggested approach here. The recommended approach is to follow an example from help and use dedicated 'mini.files' events. With something like this:\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('User', {\n  pattern = 'MiniFilesBufferCreate',\n  callback = function(args)\n    vim.keymap.set('n', '<Esc>', function() MiniFiles.close() end, { buffer = args.data.buf_id, desc = 'Close' })\n  end,\n})",
